  "body": "### Describe the bug\nAfter upgrading Homarr from **v1.74.0** to **v1.75.0**, the dashboard briefly shows skeleton/loading placeholder blocks every time the page is refreshed before the actual widgets and cards appear.\n\nThis behavior was not present in v1.74.0. After rolling back to v1.74.0, the issue disappeared immediately.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n1. Run Homarr v1.75.0.\n2. Open a dashboard/board.\n3. Refresh the page (F5 / browser refresh).\n4. Observe that the page shell/top bar appears first, while the dashboard area briefly displays skeleton placeholder blocks.\n5. Roll back to v1.74.0 and repeat the same steps.\n6. The skeleton flash no longer occurs.\n\n### Impact\nHomarr remains usable, but the skeleton placeholders flash on every refresh and make the dashboard feel noticeably less smooth. A current workaround is to pin the Docker image to `ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr:v1.74.0`.\n\n### Additional information\n- **Version with issue:** 1.75.0\n- **Version without issue:** 1.74.0\n- **Installation:** Synology Container Manager / Docker Compose\n- **Browser:** Chrome\n- `/appdata` is persisted via a bind mount.\n- Docker socket integration is disabled, so the behavior does not appear related to Docker socket access.\n- The issue is consistently reproducible on every page refresh.\n\nA screenshot was captured immediately after refresh showing the skeleton state, with the dashboard name redacted for privacy.",
